# The log of the test must have a line for each of these patterns (grep -E).
# The guard has the walking speed of its patrol before the fight
\[2\.20\].* dump Terrorist12 state=Patrolling .* DesiredSpeed=0\.296000
# It comes after the player with the "run and fire" animation and with its full speed
\[10\.60\].* dump Terrorist12 state=Attacking .* AnimSequence=RunShoot DesiredSpeed=1\.000000 GroundSpeed=200\.000000
# It runs or it strafes, each with its full speed
\[12\.60\].* dump Terrorist12 state=Attacking .* AnimSequence=(RunShoot|Strafe) DesiredSpeed=1\.000000
# It starts at X = 9. With the full speed its X position is above 500 at 12.6 seconds. With the walking speed it was
# below 250 at that time.
\[12\.60\].* dump Terrorist12 state=Attacking loc=\(([5-9][0-9][0-9]|1[0-9][0-9][0-9]) 
!dump Terrorist12 .* AnimSequence=RunShoot DesiredSpeed=0\.
# The guard went to a place from which the player is in the range of its pistol, and it fires from there.
# The fight has random parts, so the place is different for each random sequence. The distance to the player was
# between 940 and 1020 units in 4 runs.
\[19\.60\].* dump Terrorist12 state=Attacking .* dist=([89][0-9][0-9]|10[0-4][0-9]) 
# A direction test of the guard found a place
Harness: direction Terrorist12 .* dest=\(
# The guard does not play a run animation with no movement
!\[19\.60\].* dump Terrorist12 .* AnimSequence=Run.* Velocity=\(X=-?[0-9]\.[0-9]+, Y=-?[0-9]\.[0-9]+,
